    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d259">

                <pb facs="0329" n="213" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg213"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1075.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Sullivan to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santon Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-02T15:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 2, 1914, 3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your February 27, 10 p.m. Bordas intends going to Puerto Plata. He knows Arias
                    wants Vice Presidency and heavy tribute from Government receipts. Bordas asserts
                    that tentative nature and uncertainty of your proposition for funds leaves him
                    without strength he needs. With positive assurance of financial support Arias
                    could be obliterated without serious consequences; that to accede to him terms
                    which is the alternative without certainty of the Department’s position means
                    fastening him upon country as a leech. Impossible for provisional Government to
                    resist Arias in present bankruptcy. What offer would be justifiable to placate
                    Arias? State how far Department thinks Government should go and consider whether
                    Arias should be permitted to regulate elections in the north. An immediate
                    answer will save all interested from vacillation which in my opinion would be
                    most unfortunate in a situation demanding firmness and instant definite plan of
                    procedure if, which is likely, Arias is not placated; funds are needed not for
                    the future but at once.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
